 "subject": "audit: fix every defect from the 2026-08-09 full review",
 "body": "H1  All 19 CLI parsers now reject unknown flags via one shared guard.\n    Silent dropping was the mechanism behind two shipped bugs (--format on\n    map/cycles, --scope on search); 18 parsers still did it.\n\nH2  The \"verbatim, identical to Read\" claims were false since the v0.38.5\n    line clamp. Delivery header and prism_query description now state the\n    1200-char truncation and tell the agent to Read before editing a\n    truncated line.\n\nH3  prism.yaml's generated comment claimed model auto-detection from the MCP\n    initialize handshake. No such code exists \u2014 the handler reads only the\n    protocol version. The comment now says there is no auto-detection and\n    what unset actually means.\n\nH4  Tracker.Lookup returns a defensive copy (SymbolSHAs deep-copied). Five\n    call sites read entry fields after the mutex released; under the\n    concurrent HTTP server that was a data race on live structs, and the\n    same aliasing already produced the graphcache seen-count bug.\n\nH5  (found by the new pinning test) Invoke had no panic recovery: one\n    nil-pointer in one tool killed the whole stdio MCP server \u2014 the agent's\n    entire session. A panic now fails that call only.\n\nM1  The grep",
